WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.580
In early 1897, the newspaper owner
William Randolph Hearst

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.190
sent Remington to Cuba, where Cubans
were fighting for independence from Spain.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.830
Hearst wanted the country's
most famous illustrator,

4
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.130
not just a reporter.

5
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.490
And Remington didn't change in Cuba.

6
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.650
He brought the same visual logic
to a new place.

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.120
You may have heard of a famous telegram
from Hearst: You furnish the pictures,

8
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.370
and I'll furnish the war.
It is probably apocryphal.

9
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.120
It was first reported years later,
and Hearst denied it.

10
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.890
But it captures the attitude.
